# Advisories waived for the Trivy scans in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# Keep this in sync with frontend/.audit-allowlist.json — the npm audit gate
# and Trivy scan the same dependency tree, so an advisory waived in one and
# not the other just moves the red from one job to another.
#
# Trivy has no expiry mechanism, so the expiry lives with the npm waiver and
# is repeated here as a comment. Re-review both together.

# react-router — RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before 400
# Response. Not reachable: this is a client-only Vite SPA using BrowserRouter
# with no RSC mode, server actions, or react-router server runtime. No patched
# react-router-dom exists (7.18.2 is the last release and pins the vulnerable
# react-router 7.18.2); the fix ships in react-router 8.3.0, which requires
# migrating off react-router-dom. Tracked as a separate migration.
